cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these files, please cite them as below."
title: "Mechanical Design Basics: From Requirement to Release - open course files"
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: "Vijayakumar"
    family-names: "Yeddula"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3998-500X"
abstract: >-
  Open learner files of a free YouTube course on mechanical design basics (24 episodes in
  three parts: define and make it strong; drawings, tolerances and GD&T; make it buildable
  and release it). The course follows a fictional belt-driven actuator (ACT-100) and its
  sheet-metal motor bracket (ACT-103) from requirement to release. The release contains,
  for every episode, a worksheet and an answer key (PDF); reference cards; engineering
  drawings and planted-error drawing exercises (PDF); a DXF flat pattern; spreadsheet
  templates and calculators (XLSX, CSV); STEP models of the bracket at Rev A and Rev B;
  and a Python generator that computes every number used in the course, with self-checks,
  plus a shelf-bracket exercise generator. Fictional company, synthetic data.
  Educational material - verify with current standards and your supplier.
license: CC-BY-4.0
